WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.461
Every Aztec transaction

00:00:01.461 --> 00:00:02.748
pays a network fee,

00:00:02.748 --> 00:00:04.826
the way Ethereum charges gas.

00:00:04.826 --> 00:00:06.913
The fee is paid in Fee Juice,

00:00:06.913 --> 00:00:09.557
the token that pays network fees on Aztec.

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:10.878
You bring the Aztec token

00:00:10.878 --> 00:00:12.026
over from Ethereum,

00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:13.661
and it becomes Fee Juice.

00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:15.991
Once converted, it cannot be transferred,

00:00:15.991 --> 00:00:18.130
and it is used only for fees.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.043
The price depends on the work:

00:00:20.043 --> 00:00:21.643
publishing the transaction's data,

00:00:21.643 --> 00:00:23.348
and running it on the network.

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:25.991
Nulo shows you the fee before you send.

00:00:25.991 --> 00:00:27.661
How you pay matters.

00:00:27.661 --> 00:00:29.052
Pay with public Fee Juice,

00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:31.174
and the record names you as the payer,

00:00:31.174 --> 00:00:32.043
each time.

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:33.539
Pay with private Fee Juice,

00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:34.826
and the payer on record is a

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:36.843
contract many people share.

00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:38.861
Sometimes the fee is sponsored:

00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:40.487
someone else pays it for you.

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:43.130
Nulo always tells you how the fee is paid,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.470
and you are always in control.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.417
Fees are paid in Fee Juice,

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:48.739
and how you pay decides

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:49.991
what the record shows.
